013","fg:item:000454:event:0014","fg:item:000454:event:0015","fg:item:000454:event:0016","fg:item:000454:event:0017","fg:item:000454:event:0018","fg:item:000454:event:0019","fg:item:000454:event:0020","fg:item:000454:event:0021","fg:item:000454:event:0022","fg:item:000454:event:0023","fg:item:000454:event:0024","fg:item:000454:event:0025","fg:item:000454:event:0026","fg:item:000454:event:0027","fg:item:000454:event:0028","fg:item:000454:event:0029","fg:item:000454:event:0030","fg:item:000454:event:0031","fg:item:000454:event:0032"],"grouping":{"beat_unit_q":null,"kind":"even_subdivision","marking_factor":[1,1],"notes_per_beat":3,"source_label":"triplets per authored session grouping"},"id":"fg:variant:003401","label":"triplets-up_and_down-U-even","pick_start":"U","pick_start_origin":"source_authored","role":"notation_practice","route":"up_and_down","source_refs":["L4-TXT1-22","L4-PDF1","L4-TXT25-25","L4-TXT188-202"],"tail_pause":null,"unresolved":["Authored grouping count retained; explicit metrical beat-unit configuration required."]}],"workbook_id":"fg:workbook:000004"}],"schema_version":"1.0.0-curriculum-candidate","source_acceptance":"Results/primary/20260906T182131Z-2.1.1.1.1-r02-results.md","source_manifest_sha256":"e856ef05e610b9be51f33aac661a900301f747a9259bfcbd951b756a247504fe","sources":{"L4-PDF1":{"format":"pdf","page":1,"path":"Notes/music/guitar project/PDF version/108_Finger_Permutations_Level_4_Three_String_Relay.pdf","sha256":"b24cad79148b8165b74cbd3662031c2ad0227f0e856aa955d03c88db31dbafb1","text":"108 Finger Permutations - Level 4\nThree-String Relay: 1+2+1 Two-Crossing Control\nLevel 3 moved one adjacent-string crossing. Level 4 adds a second crossing while keeping the fret position and string spacing fixed.\n1. Same fretting map\n1 = index / fret 5\n2 = middle / fret 6\n3 = ring / fret 7\n4 = pinky / fret 8\nThe four-digit code stays unchanged.\n2. New movement rule\nCode note 1: first string\nCode notes 2-3: middle string\nCode note 4: third string\nMove through adjacent three-string groups.\nThere is still no string skip.\n3. Picking objective\nCrossings occur after notes 1 and 3.\nA downstroke start makes both landings upstrokes.\nAn upstroke start makes both landings downstrokes.\nKeep both landings even and relaxed.\nMute every unused string.\nWorked example - code 1234\nPlay note 1 on the first string, notes 2-3 on the middle string, and note 4 on the third string.\nASCEND: E/A/D -> G/B/e\ne|--------|--------|--------|------8-|\nB|--------|--------|------8-|--6-7---|\nG|--------|------8-|--6-7---|5-------|\nD|------8-|--6-7---|5-------|--------|\nA|--6-7---|5-------|--------|--------|\nE|5-------|--------|--------|--------|\nDESCEND: e/B/G -> D/A/E\ne|5-------|--------|--------|--------|\nB|--6-7---|5-------|--------|--------|\nG|------8-|--6-7---|5-------|--------|\nD|--------|------8-|--6-7---|5-------|\nA|--------|--------|------8-|--6-7---|\nE|--------|--------|--------|------8-|\nFIRST PASS\nLightly accent landing notes 2 and 4 so both crossings are deliberate.\nSECOND PASS\nRemove the accents and make all four notes equal in volume and duration.\nPlay ASCEND directly into DESCEND without resetting the hands or the pick.\nPractice protocol\n1\nChoose one 12-exercise set.\n2\nStart 10-15 BPM below your clean\nLevel 3 tempo.\n3\nPlay ASCEND directly into DESCEND.\n4\nRepeat with the opposite starting\npick stroke.\n5\nFirst accent notes 2 and 4; then\nequalize all four notes.\n6\nThree clean loops: add 2 BPM\nnext session.\n7\nTwo errors or rising tension:\nreduce 4-6 BPM.\nAdvance after the complete set is clean with both pick starts\non two separate days.\nStandard tuning. Fifth position. 1+2+1 across three adjacent strings; no string skip or position shift.\nPage 1 of 10\n","text_sha256":"ba7d21ec9887b3af510c22ffc3ce55134c0351e73e0e3caa14a91cbad0ed0846"},"L4-TXT1-22":{"first_line":1,"format":"txt","last_line":22,"path":"Notes/music/guitar project/TXT version/108_Finger_Permutations_Level_4_Three_String_Relay.txt","sha256":"4c90d79866f42125a7aa8785e803462864dbb88b2ecfa856438bf49f922f3d9a","text":"108 FINGER PERMUTATIONS - LEVEL 4: THREE-STRING RELAY\n1+2+1 two-crossing control in standard tuning.\nFifth position: 1=index/fret 5, 2=middle/fret 6, 3=ring/fret 7, 4=pinky/fret 8.\n\nMOVEMENT RULE\nFor every adjacent three-string group, play code note 1 on the first string, code notes 2-3 on the middle string,\nand code note 4 on the third string. The 1+2+1 description refers to note counts, not finger numbers.\nAscend through E/A/D, A/D/G, D/G/B, G/B/e. Descend through e/B/G, B/G/D, G/D/A, D/A/E.\nThe four-digit code order never changes. There is no string skip or position shift yet.\n\nWHY THIS IS LEVEL 4\nLevels 2 and 3 used one adjacent-string crossing per four-note code. Level 4 adds a second crossing.\nWith a downstroke start, notes 2 and 4 land on upstrokes. With an upstroke start, both land on downstrokes.\nPracticing both starts exposes both pick-escape directions while the fretting position remains fixed.\n\nPRACTICE RULE\nUse one 12-exercise set per session. Start 10-15 BPM below your clean Level 3 tempo.\nPlay ASCEND directly into DESCEND, then repeat the entire exercise with the opposite starting pick stroke.\nFirst pass: lightly accent landing notes 2 and 4. Second pass: make all four notes equal in volume and duration.\nUse straight 16ths first. Reintroduce triplet and quintuplet groupings only after the crossings are stable.\nAfter three clean loops, add 2 BPM next session. After two errors or rising tension, reduce 4-6 BPM.\nAdvance after the full set is clean with both pick starts on two separate days.","text_sha256":"4a85d074421c73f93acf1905a684dc4d6b3ab41c8d339ca801081228bd138d8c"},"L4-TXT188-202":{"first_line":188,"format":"txt","last_line":202,"path":"Notes/music/guitar project/TXT version/108_Finger_Permutations_Level_4_Three_String_Relay.txt","sha256":"4c90d79866f42125a7aa8785e803462864dbb88b2ecfa856438bf49f922f3d9a","text":"Exercise 011: 1313\nASCEND\ne|--------|--------|--------|------7-|\nB|--------|--------|------7-|--7-5---|\nG|--------|------7-|--7-5---|5-------|\nD|------7-|--7-5---|5-------|--------|\nA|--7-5---|5-------|--------|--------|\nE|5-------|--------|--------|--------|\nDESCEND\ne|5-------|--------|--------|--------|\nB|--7-5---|5-------|--------|--------|\nG|------7-|--7-5---|5-------|--------|\nD|--------|------7-|--7-5---|5-------|\nA|--------|--------|------7-|--7-5---|\nE|--------|--------|--------|------7-|","text_sha256":"2e98689743d9ad21a781bfa96a4691027196630318fb788c9f40f124f34dc6e0"},"L4-TXT25-25":{"first_line":25,"format":"txt","last_line":25,"path":"Notes/music/guitar project/TXT version/108_Finger_Permutations_Level_4_Three_String_Relay.txt","sha256":"4c90d79866f42125a7aa8785e803462864dbb88b2ecfa856438bf49f922f3d9a","text":"SET 1 OF 9 - EXERCISES 001-012","text_sha256":"239b1881cfc47b7066c6e07958e765815a8d0c156dd3f618706dc2d55330e51a"}}},"reference_registry":{"entities":[{"id":"fg:course:000001","kind":"course","label":"Fathom Guitar105","parent":null},{"id":"fg:workbook:000004","kind":"workbook","label":"Level4 three-string relay","parent":"fg:course:000001"},{"id":"fg:module:000454","kind":"module","label":"Exercise011 1313","parent":"fg:workbook:000004"},{"id":"fg:item:000454","kind":"item","label":"Exercise011 1313 up and down","parent":"fg:module:000454"},{"id":"fg:variant:003394","kind":"variant","label":"sixteenths-up_and_down-D-after_crossing","parent":"fg:item:000454"},{"id":"fg:variant:003395","kind":"variant","label":"sixteenths-up_and_down-D-even","parent":"fg:item:000454"},{"id":"fg:variant:003396","kind":"variant","label":"sixteenths-up_and_down-U-after_crossing","parent":"fg:item:000454"},{"id":"fg:variant:003397","kind":"variant","label":"sixteenths-up_and_down-U-even","parent":"fg:item:000454"},{"id":"fg:variant:003398","kind":"variant","label":"triplets-up_and_down-D-after_crossing","parent":"fg:item:000454"},{"id":"fg:variant:003399","kind":"variant